Mini data protection by design checklist

Scope: Highest-risk activity — extracting, scoring and ranking EU/EEA job applicants.

Control

Status

Current finding

Required next step

Data minimisation

Fail

The proposed flow can send the full CV and free text, although photographs, addresses, affiliations and other fields may be irrelevant to suitability.

Define a job-relevance schema, redact excluded fields before the API call, and prohibit sensitive/proxy features.

Purpose binding

Unknown

The intended baseline forbids training, but vendor retention settings and downstream contractual restrictions are not yet evidenced.

Apply the no-training clause, disable retention/training technically, verify sub-processors and retain configuration evidence.

Access controls

Unknown

Authorised recruiter and support roles are described, but least-privilege roles, MFA, access reviews and audit-log testing are not evidenced.

Implement role-based access, MFA, quarterly access review and alerting for bulk or unusual access.

Retention enforcement

Fail

A schedule exists, but automated deletion across production, API records, logs and backups has not been demonstrated.

Implement deletion jobs, vendor deletion instructions, backup expiry and quarterly deletion testing.

Subject-rights workflow

Unknown

Applicants need access, correction, objection, erasure/restriction and human-review routes, but no tested 30-day case workflow exists.

Create one intake channel, ownership matrix, identity verification, processor search/export support and deadline alerts; run a tabletop test.

Incident response

Unknown

Article 28 breach support is required, but detection, escalation and evidence needed for the controller's 72-hour assessment are not documented.

Adopt an incident playbook, agree rapid processor-to-controller notice, maintain contact details and test a CV-data breach scenario.

Overall result: Do not launch yet. The design can move to controlled pilot only after both failures are remediated, unknowns are evidenced, the DPIA is approved and a no-auto-rejection workflow is tested.

